# Only what the build needs is sent to Docker. Everything is left out first, and then the Go
# module, the server's packages, the web client and the image's default settings are let back in.
# A new top-level Go package has to be added here: the build fails without it.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!main.go
!auth
!cmd
!diskcache
!errors
!files
!fileutils
!frontend
!http
!img
!rules
!runner
!search
!settings
!share
!storage
!users
!version
!docker/defaults

# Local files that must not reach a build, wherever they are: secrets such as the .env file that
# Compose reads, databases, backups, and files that would only make the build run again. These
# come after the lines above, because the last pattern that matches a file decides.
**/.env*
**/*.db
**/*.db.*
**/*.bak
**/.DS_Store
**/*.md

# Build output. The image installs the client's dependencies and builds the client itself.
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/test-results
